@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/road#> .
@prefix courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph ;    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is
    owl:imports <../courier/ontology.ttl> ,    # the words the road is laid out in: a cell and its coordinates
                <constraints.ttl> .            # and what no van on it does, which a world's agents hold

#  THE ROAD, A DOMAIN.
#  One stretch of road, shared by every world posed on it: a single-track lane with a passing place, open
#  road two cells wide at each end. The road is its cells, each its two coordinates and nothing else - a
#  neighbour is a cell one away on one axis, which the drive's own precondition works out from the
#  coordinates, so the road declares no edge (#1012, refused). What it is NOT is a world: it says nothing of
#  who drives on it, where a van stands or what is owed where. `world/lane/` poses two couriers on it,
#  `world/layby/` one courier and a van parked by a driver nobody plays, the same road under different
#  initial states; a third world would import this document and author its vans.
#
#  THE SHAPE: columns 0 and 1 and columns 5 and 6 are open road, three rows deep; columns 2 to 4 are the
#  lane, row 1 alone, and (3, 2) is the passing place. A cell is its two coordinates, which is what a van's
#  fix reports and what a van is told: an instrument gives numbers, and the coordinates are the courier's
#  own (knowledge/domain/courier/position.md). The grid is infinite, a cell being any pair of coordinates, and
#  the road is the part of it these worlds' agents know: a plan is searched over the cells an agent knows,
#  so a van is driven along the road because its courier knows no other cell, not because the world refuses.

#  Western road
:c0_0 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 0 ; courier:y 0 .
:c0_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 0 ; courier:y 1 .
:c0_2 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 0 ; courier:y 2 .
:c1_0 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 1 ; courier:y 0 .
:c1_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 1 ; courier:y 1 .
:c1_2 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 1 ; courier:y 2 .
#  The lane, and its passing place
:c2_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 2 ; courier:y 1 .
:c3_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 3 ; courier:y 1 .
:c3_2 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 3 ; courier:y 2 ; rdfs:label "the passing place" .
:c4_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 4 ; courier:y 1 .
#  Eastern road
:c5_0 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 5 ; courier:y 0 .
:c5_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 5 ; courier:y 1 .
:c5_2 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 5 ; courier:y 2 .
:c6_0 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 6 ; courier:y 0 .
:c6_1 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 6 ; courier:y 1 .
:c6_2 a courier:Cell ; courier:x 6 ; courier:y 2 .
